## DESIGN PRINCIPLES (Apply to All Layers)

**Minimal**: Remove all non-essential elements. Every pixel serves a purpose.

**Consistent**: Reuse spacing, colors, typography across all components and screens.

**Accessible**: WCAG 2.1 AA compliance by default. Test with screen readers.

**Responsive**: Mobile-first design. Scale gracefully to tablet & desktop.

**Performant**: Optimize SVGs. Use CSS animations, not JavaScript.

**Documented**: Every component has usage guidelines, do's & don'ts, code examples.

**On-Brand**: Use atlas.core palette, typography, mark, and tone consistently.

---

## EXECUTION STRATEGY (Token Optimization)

**Batch similar work**: Design all icons at once, not one at a time.

**Reuse patterns**: Build components from icons and tokens. Don't reinvent.

**Show, don't tell**: Use visuals (charts, icons, mockups) instead of long descriptions.

**Minimal copy**: Specs are concise. Code examples are short. No fluff.

**Figma as source**: Design once in Figma, export to SVG/PNG/code.

**Semantic naming**: Use consistent naming conventions (e.g., `button-primary`, `spacing-16`, `color-ink`).

